 "notes": [
  {
   "id": "np15-01",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Characterisation",
   "quote": "Hannibalis praecepto",
   "trans": "on Hannibal's instructions",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Even in the heat of battle the Bithynians act on Hannibal's orders, which keeps him at the centre of the victory.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-02",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Emphasis",
   "quote": "universi",
   "trans": "all together",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Every Bithynian ship attacks the king's, exactly as Hannibal ordered: the plan works to the letter.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-03",
   "cat": "order",
   "label": "Emphatic position",
   "quote": "navem Eumenis adoriuntur",
   "trans": "they attack Eumenes' ship",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The target and the attack end the sentence, and the historic present adoriuntur makes the onslaught vivid.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-04",
   "cat": "structure",
   "label": "Contrast",
   "quote": "vim … fuga salutem petiit",
   "trans": "the attack … sought safety in flight",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Unable to withstand the force, the king looks for safety in flight: Rome's proud ally is reduced to running away.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-05",
   "cat": "grammar",
   "label": "Conditional",
   "quote": "quam consecutus non esset, nisi … se recepisset",
   "trans": "he would not have reached it, had he not retreated",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The past unreal condition shows how narrow his escape was: only his defences on the shore saved him.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-06",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Vivid detail",
   "quote": "premerent acrius",
   "trans": "were pressing harder",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The rest of the Pergamene fleet is winning, which makes the sudden reversal more striking.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-07",
   "cat": "order",
   "label": "Emphatic position",
   "quote": "repente",
   "trans": "suddenly",
   "line": "",
   "body": "repente comes before the pots are named, so the reader feels the surprise before seeing the weapon.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-08",
   "cat": "structure",
   "label": "Narrator's aside",
   "quote": "de quibus supra mentionem fecimus",
   "trans": "which I mentioned above",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Nepos reminds the reader of the pots from chapter 10. The reader, unlike the Pergamenes, knows what is inside them.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-09",
   "cat": "imagery",
   "label": "Dramatic irony",
   "quote": "risum pugnantibus concitarunt",
   "trans": "they made the fighting men laugh",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The Pergamenes laugh at clay pots as weapons, but the reader knows what they hold, so the laughter is short-lived.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-10",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Emphasis",
   "quote": "initio",
   "trans": "at first",
   "line": "",
   "body": "\"At first\" signals that the mood is about to change.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-11",
   "cat": "order",
   "label": "Hyperbaton",
   "quote": "naves suas oppletas conspexerunt serpentibus",
   "trans": "they saw their ships filled with snakes",
   "line": "",
   "body": "serpentibus is separated from oppletas and held back to the end of the clause, so the snakes arrive as a shock.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-12",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Emphasis",
   "quote": "nova re perterriti",
   "trans": "utterly terrified by something new",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The prefix per- and the word nova (\"unheard of\") explain the panic: nothing had prepared them for this.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-13",
   "cat": "grammar",
   "label": "Indirect question",
   "quote": "quid potissimum vitarent, non viderent",
   "trans": "they could not see what they should most avoid",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Snakes on board and enemies all round: the sailors cannot decide which danger is worse, which shows total confusion.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-14",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Vivid detail",
   "quote": "puppes verterunt",
   "trans": "they turned their sterns",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Turning the sterns is a vivid way of saying they fled, the opposite of facing the enemy.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-15",
   "cat": "structure",
   "label": "Antithesis",
   "quote": "consilio arma",
   "trans": "by planning … arms",
   "line": "",
   "body": "Strategy defeats weapons: two words set side by side sum up the episode.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-16",
   "cat": "structure",
   "label": "Contrast",
   "quote": "neque tum solum, sed saepe alias",
   "trans": "not only then but often on other occasions",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The general statement widens the episode into proof of Hannibal's genius on land as well as at sea.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-17",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Characterisation",
   "quote": "pari prudentia",
   "trans": "with equal skill",
   "line": "",
   "body": "prudentia recalls chapter 1, where Hannibal surpasses all other generals in prudentia: the episode confirms Nepos' first judgement.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-18",
   "cat": "note",
   "label": "Bithynians",
   "quote": "Bithynii",
   "trans": "the Bithynians",
   "line": "",
   "body": "The subjects of Prusias, from Bithynia in north-west Asia Minor, between the Sea of Marmara and the Black Sea.",
   "exam": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "np15-19",
   "cat": "note",
   "label": "Pergamum",
   "quote": "Pergamenae",
   "trans": "Pergamene",
   "line": "",
   "body": "From Pergamum, Eumenes' capital in north-west Asia Minor, one of the richest Hellenistic kingdoms and Rome's chief ally in the region.",
   "exam": ""
  }
 ],
 "section": 15,
 "questions": [
  "Nepos ends the episode by generalising about Hannibal's skill. How does this chapter support the claims made about Hannibal in chapter 1?",
  "How does Nepos turn a battle narrative into something close to comedy, and why might he do so?",
  "Is the victory at sea a victory of courage or of cunning? Does Nepos seem to see any difference?"
 ]
}